autocatalyst formulations.  The quantity of palladium used in autocatalyst production thus depends on seven overlapping factors:- 

- World vehicle production, and the regional breakdown of sales (particularly how fast the markets of China, India and Brazil expand vis-а-vis those in the developed world); 

- Emissions legislation (tighter standards almost always require higher metal loadings); 

- Engine capacities (since allowable emission limits are set per distance travelled rather than per unit of fuel consumed, large-engine vehicles must transform a greater proportion of their higher waste gas streams, and so use larger catalysts); 

- Engine type (since palladium is cheaper than platinum, this tends to be used wherever technically feasible, but it can be poisoned by diesel emissions so catalysts for such vehicles have historically been more platinum-rich); 

